you press Ctrl+Z, the process is paused/frozen — it's still in memory, just not running.

Restart a Stopped Process

fg      # resume it in the foreground (you can see its output)
bg      # resume it in the background (runs silently)

Simple Example

python3 script.py       # start a process
# press Ctrl+Z
# [1]+  Stopped    python3 script.py

fg                      # resumes it
# OR
bg                      # resumes it in background

If You Have Multiple Stopped Processes

jobs                    # list all stopped processes
# [1]+  Stopped    python3 script.py
# [2]-  Stopped    bash myscript.sh

fg %1                   # resume job number 1
fg %2                   # resume job number 2

Key Point

Ctrl+Z = pause (like pausing a video) → fg/bg = play again

It does NOT kill the process — the process is still there in memory, just frozen. fg and bg unfreeze it.